{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "ee164a1a-32c0-5adf-b341-fe20e94f7608",
  "Description": "A wall of 80 bricks from one RigidBody, knocked down by a heavy block.\n\n[GridPoints] lays out the wall and [ReadPointsFromGpu] hands the points to the Points input of a single [RigidBody], which becomes one body per point. A second, heavy [RigidBody] is thrown at it with LinearVelocity.\n\nAKA: pyramid, colosseum, stack, instances, bodies from points\n\nTips\n- Change the counts on [GridPoints] to build a bigger wall; no other node changes.\n- Set Reset on [PhysicsWorld] to rebuild the wall.\n- All bodies of a world share one point buffer, so they are drawn with one mesh: the projectile is a box too.",
